{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DLN9vCB2MB6A45tmpCj5Vf","type":"tool_result","content":"506:- `game.start({ boot })`: { title, version, steps: [[label, fn]], messages, min, checks, accent } runs the boot first (section 10c): the steps one a frame behind the boot screen (all at once when headless or loop: false); boot: false hides a splash\n516:- `game.bootError = null`: the error a boot step failed with (the game did not start), or null\n517:- `game.booted`: a promise of the game once its boot (start's boot option, section 10c) has run and it has started: await it in a test whose boot steps return promises\n560:- `E.showError(title, e)`: show an error in the red box at the top of the page (the engine does it for errors in update and draw); a click hides it. Before play has started it shows on the boot screen instead, as a report a player can screenshot\n581:- `E.bootSplash(title = '')`: the boot screen's markup, for the very start of a page's <body>: it shows from the first paint, its bar moving while the page's scripts load (a pure CSS animation), and says so if the game's script never runs. The engine takes it over\n582:- `E.diagnose(game = E.current)`: the report a bug needs, at any time (and on the boot screen when a game can't start): { engine, game, time, page, browser, device, screen, canvas, gpu, sound, storage, input, scene, errors, text (all of it, one line each, for a screenshot or a bug report), short (one line) }. game: the game to report on (E.current)\n679:- `rig.C`: its colors (skin, hair, cloth, pants, boot, belt, cape, capeIn, metal, hilt, eye, ...), the defaults with o.colors over them; change one and it shows at the next draw\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71d84256-7fc9-49b2-a3c8-c6f9b5cc892b","uuid":"92a00167-7a74-4d5a-997c-b11a0e363fc9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:28:15.387Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"506:- `game.start({ boot })`: { title, version, steps: [[label, fn]], messages, min, checks, accent } runs the boot first (section 10c): the steps one a frame behind the boot screen (all at once when headless or loop: false); boot: false hides a splash\n516:- `game.bootError = null`: the error a boot step failed with (the game did not start), or null\n517:- `game.booted`: a promise of the game once its boot (start's boot option, section 10c) has run and it has started: await it in a test whose boot steps return promises\n560:- `E.showError(title, e)`: show an error in the red box at the top of the page (the engine does it for errors in update and draw); a click hides it. Before play has started it shows on the boot screen instead, as a report a player can screenshot\n581:- `E.bootSplash(title = '')`: the boot screen's markup, for the very start of a page's <body>: it shows from the first paint, its bar moving while the page's scripts load (a pure CSS animation), and says so if the game's script never runs. The engine takes it over\n582:- `E.diagnose(game = E.current)`: the report a bug needs, at any time (and on the boot screen when a game can't start): { engine, game, time, page, browser, device, screen, canvas, gpu, sound, storage, input, scene, errors, text (all of it, one line each, for a screenshot or a bug report), short (one line) }. game: the game to report on (E.current)\n679:- `rig.C`: its colors (skin, hair, cloth, pants, boot, belt, cape, capeIn, metal, hilt, eye, ...), the defaults with o.colors over them; change one and it shows at the next draw\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DLN9vCB2MB6A45tmpCj5Vf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
