{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghwp348KAvLtMLj6nYvd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013pm2opzFTQEpUsxnteaenb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'; cat > engine/CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Changes CRACKMANIA made to my-3D2dge v0.85.2\n\n| # | File | Change | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| E1 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `Pen` | `pen.frame(x, y, z, f, r, u, k)`: the pen's frame from forward/right/up vectors | draw a car in any orientation (upside down in a loop) without Euler angles |\n| E2 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `Camera3D.place()` | a pose may carry `up: [x, y, z]` (engine axes); roll is skipped then | a chase camera that rolls with the car round a loop |\n| E3 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `makeBatches()` + `Pen` | four translucent toon batches (`gbox`, `gball`, `gtube`, `gcone`); `pen.ghost = true` routes parts into them | TrackMania's see-through ghost cars, with materials made once with the world |\n| E4 | `my-3d2dge.js`, `Input.tick` / `analog()` | keeps each pad button's value; `input.analog(action)` returns 0..1 (a trigger's travel, 1 for a held key) | analog R2 throttle and L2 brake |\n| E5 | `my-3d2dge.js`, input + settings | button symbols default to PlayStation; the setting offers PlayStation / Xbox | TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs, Xbox by setting |\n| E6 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, statics | `World3D.TOON_BANDS` and `World3D.lambert(map)` exported | track and prop materials in the engine's own toon bands |\n\n`tools/engine-patch.py` applies E1-E6 to fresh copies of the two engine files.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# CRACKMANIA (dev folder)\n\n- Build the single file: `npm install` (esbuild, Playwright), then `node tools/build.mjs` -> `../Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050311.html` and `../exit-interview.json` (from `src/info.json`).\n- Test: `node tools/test.mjs` (headless suites, prints failures and one count line); `--browser` adds the Playwright checks of the built file, `--hub` the AI Hub harness (3 scenarios), `--all` both.\n- Look: `node tools/shot.mjs <name> \"<js>;;wait:ms;;key:Enter;;shot:name\"` screenshots the built file into `check-output/`.\n- Source: `src/` (ES modules; `main.js` is the game), engine copies in `engine/` (changes in `engine/CHANGES.md`), the AI Hub client in `hub/session.js` (verbatim).\n- Content: tracks are turtle programs in `src/data.js`; Dev Mode's \"Export as content\" prints an editor track in the same placement format.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write engine CHANGES.md and dev README"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2240,"cache_read_input_tokens":616091,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2240},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71d84256-7fc9-49b2-a3c8-c6f9b5cc892b","uuid":"e50a5d45-8b74-4623-9ac2-3b4b322a2a38","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:12:40.327Z","request_id":"req_011Cghwp2f4kXWRhF5uzYabV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013pm2opzFTQEpUsxnteaenb":{"command":"date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'; cat > engine/CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Changes CRACKMANIA made to my-3D2dge v0.85.2\n\n| # | File | Change | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| E1 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `Pen` | `pen.frame(x, y, z, f, r, u, k)`: the pen's frame from forward/right/up vectors | draw a car in any orientation (upside down in a loop) without Euler angles |\n| E2 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `Camera3D.place()` | a pose may carry `up: [x, y, z]` (engine axes); roll is skipped then | a chase camera that rolls with the car round a loop |\n| E3 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `makeBatches()` + `Pen` | four translucent toon batches (`gbox`, `gball`, `gtube`, `gcone`); `pen.ghost = true` routes parts into them | TrackMania's see-through ghost cars, with materials made once with the world |\n| E4 | `my-3d2dge.js`, `Input.tick` / `analog()` | keeps each pad button's value; `input.analog(action)` returns 0..1 (a trigger's travel, 1 for a held key) | analog R2 throttle and L2 brake |\n| E5 | `my-3d2dge.js`, input + settings | button symbols default to PlayStation; the setting offers PlayStation / Xbox | TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs, Xbox by setting |\n| E6 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, statics | `World3D.TOON_BANDS` and `World3D.lambert(map)` exported | track and prop materials in the engine's own toon bands |\n\n`tools/engine-patch.py` applies E1-E6 to fresh copies of the two engine files.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# CRACKMANIA (dev folder)\n\n- Build the single file: `npm install` (esbuild, Playwright), then `node tools/build.mjs` -> `../Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050311.html` and `../exit-interview.json` (from `src/info.json`).\n- Test: `node tools/test.mjs` (headless suites, prints failures and one count line); `--browser` adds the Playwright checks of the built file, `--hub` the AI Hub harness (3 scenarios), `--all` both.\n- Look: `node tools/shot.mjs <name> \"<js>;;wait:ms;;key:Enter;;shot:name\"` screenshots the built file into `check-output/`.\n- Source: `src/` (ES modules; `main.js` is the game), engine copies in `engine/` (changes in `engine/CHANGES.md`), the AI Hub client in `hub/session.js` (verbatim).\n- Content: tracks are turtle programs in `src/data.js`; Dev Mode's \"Export as content\" prints an editor track in the same placement format.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write engine CHANGES.md and dev README"}}}
